{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/482747-question-on-new-trinity-continuum","id":482747,"title":"question on new trinity continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T13:59:36-07:00","id":482747,"title":"question on new trinity continuum","content":"So, as i have aged i have come to really.. dislike some things that i enjoyed in my younger days of gaming. Specifically super special NPCs and metaplot. Both of these things were tantamount in early WW products, and T/A/A! was initially designed during this time. <br /> <br /> Now due to the nature of this project, the second can't really be completely avoided, although much better simply deal with it in each core book rather than the classic treadmill of supplements of ages past. But the npc problem... I mean ideally Mercer and the rest of those guys will get a blurb here or there and that will be the end of it, followed by rules how to give my character super special powers that no one else can get (time travel...). Really it's just that I have gotten tired of that feeling that my character is playing in someone elses story, and lots of unavoidable signature characters does just that. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5611-cyberspidermancer","name":"cyberspidermancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T15:02:33-07:00","id":482834,"title":"","content":"So what's your question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:04:25-07:00","id":482957,"title":"","content":"But that is the beauty of roleplay. You do not need to adhere to continuity. It is, even the books say, a guideline. If you do not want metaplot, then do not include it. If you do not want powerful signature characters, then rewrite them to something that is compatible with your table and the story you want to tell. <br /> I had a buddy of mine sit down and had novas start showing up in the World of Darkness.<br /> Other people have had Exalts show up in Scion.<br /> These are examples of how you can take the setting and make it yours. There is nothing saying you have to have a metaplot. The books are there to spur ideas. They are not bibles, they are just polite and thought out suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T21:47:59-07:00","id":483161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/482747-question-on-new-trinity-continuum?p=482834#post482834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's your question?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think sometimes &quot;question&quot; and &quot;complaint&quot; tend to get conflated in certain types of online areas.<br /> <br /> I believe we will not be seeing a return of the meta-plot to with the new games, although it's too early to tell. The concept seems unpopular enough that I don't see anyone trying to revive it. As for signature characters, firstly, don't make a big deal about them - they should be examples, not straight jackets, and definitely not too special to break - and secondly, once again, I doubt that's the direction Onyx Path is gonna go, since problems with Aberrant's overuse of sig characters seems to be pretty well noted.<br /> <br /> It's really too early to have any complaints about the game so far though, when they haven't even hammered out the basic system yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:03:39-07:00","id":483517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/482747-question-on-new-trinity-continuum?p=483161#post483161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we will not be seeing a return of the meta-plot to with the new games, although it's too early to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian has clarified this before by saying 'there is no metaplot'. See comments in this thread: <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/u/0/+ChrisHill/posts/eh7dBthG9ZY\" target=\"_blank\">https://plus.google.com/u/0/+ChrisHi...ts/eh7dBthG9ZY</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}